    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a mixed slate today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (75.27) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.93). **Gunnar Henderson** remains our cornerstone play; despite facing an elite catcher and an opposing pitcher with decent metrics, his spot in the #2 hole and his dynamic platoon advantage make him our highest-projected contributor. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against a middle-of-the-road arm, with his projection bolstered by high-leverage lineup placement. **Nolan Schanuel** (67.16) rounds out our top-tier plays, as he enjoys a significant boost from a soft matchup against Trey Gibson, who holds a concerning 5.27 xERA.\n\nTactical adjustments today favor players with specific platoon or park advantages. **Cole Carrigg** (60.28) receives a notable lift from a 14% park factor, making him an efficient start despite facing a tough lefty in Ranger Suarez. Conversely, we are keeping **Jacob Wilson** (59.19) on the bench; while his projection is competitive with our MI slot, he narrowly missed the cut because the optimizer preferred the slightly higher stability of **Brayan Rocchio** (59.37) and the specific platoon benefits inherent in the latter\u2019s matchup. We are closely monitoring the 32% rain risk hovering over the contest involving **Brayan Rocchio**; should that game trend toward a postponement, **Jacob Wilson** is the immediate pivot to ensure we maximize our daily caps. While **Kyle Tucker** (53.01) and **Jackson Merrill** (55.00) are playing, their scores reflect the difficulty of facing Joe Ryan and Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, respectively, though both possess enough underlying talent to outperform these projections if they catch a favorable wind or mistake pitch.",
